Refactored the codebase from a single demo-oriented file into a reusable tree implementation plus a separate entry point. The old [avl_tree_insertion.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/044_avl_tree_insertion/avl_tree_insertion.java:1) was replaced by [AVLTree.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/044_avl_tree_insertion/AVLTree.java:5) and [AVLTreeDemo.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/044_avl_tree_insertion/AVLTreeDemo.java:1).

Key structural changes:
- [AVLTree.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/044_avl_tree_insertion/AVLTree.java:5) is now a generic `AVLTree<T>` instead of a hard-coded integer demo.
- Public tree operations are explicit: `insert`, `contains`, `size`, `isEmpty`, `preOrderTraversal`, and `preOrderString` at [AVLTree.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/044_avl_tree_insertion/AVLTree.java:31).
- Insertion now uses an internal `InsertResult` at [AVLTree.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/044_avl_tree_insertion/AVLTree.java:21), which avoids global state and cleanly tracks duplicate inserts.
- Rebalancing at [AVLTree.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/044_avl_tree_insertion/AVLTree.java:117) no longer depends on the last inserted key; it uses subtree balance information, which is a better base for future operations like deletion.
- The executable sample moved into [AVLTreeDemo.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/044_avl_tree_insertion/AVLTreeDemo.java:5), so the data structure is no longer coupled to `main`.

